> Which roguelike is considered the easiest?

The design goal of all roguelikes is to be so hard they
stay interesting for decades.  The best roguelike is
therefore the one that is the most viciously riduculously
meanly yet systematically difficult.  In other words you
want the worst, least advanced roguelike around.  Maybe
MicroRogue for Palm, maybe a very old version of Hack.

Realistically any of the popular graphical games that
were inspired by roguelikes can be played hack-n-slash.
They are all much easier than any current roguelike.
Play one of them for a year, and then come back when it
is easy and dull.  We'll still be here playing our
absurdly difficult roguelikes.



